#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Phase 8.12: the brand mirror is checked against rnv-brand installed at its pin.

What it changes (six whole files, replaced):
  tests/requirements-dev.txt
      Adds rnv-brand @ git+https://github.com/RNVizion/rnv-brand@108213b...
      (rnv-brand 48.1.0, which installs as rnv_brand). Test-only: the Space
      installs requirements.txt and nothing here.
  tests/test_brand_mirror.py
      SYNCED_SHA moves to 108213b. Seven tests: the register is installed as
      rnv_brand; this repository still reads its own engine; the pin is a full
      commit; the three pins agree; pip installed the pinned commit; the
      mirror carries the register at its pin (all 33 keys and the 11
      constants); and a named positive control for that comparison.
  engine/brand_vocab.py
      Docstring only: "Mirrored from rnv-brand@108213b...", and why. No key,
      value or code moves.
  scripts/check_brand_currency.py
      --mode transcription reads the installed rnv_brand.brand, checks that pip
      installed the pinned commit and that the imported module is that
      installation's file with the hash pip recorded, and compares every key and value exactly and every color
      constant the mirror defines, with no fetch. --mode currency still fetches upstream HEAD over
      HTTPS and parses it with ast; its value comparison is now exact too.
  .github/workflows/tests.yml
      The "mirror matches its pinned commit" job (a required check; its name
      is unchanged) installs tests/requirements-dev.txt, then runs the script.
      Any non-zero exit fails.
  .github/workflows/sync-hf.yml
      The deploy gate's mirror step: any non-zero exit fails.

Suite 553 -> 560 on Python 3.12 and 3.13. It never stages, commits or pushes.

Run from the repository root, on a branch cut from main@40589e0:
    python 01_phase_8_12.py --check    # report only
    python 01_phase_8_12.py            # write
Run it again: a second run changes nothing. Then reinstall the test
requirements (pip install -r tests/requirements-dev.txt) and run the suite.
Delete this script afterwards; it is not part of the repository.
"""
